          "worked": "Use row headers $1,2,3,4,5,6$ for the first die and column headers $1,2,3,4,5,6$ for the second die. Each body cell contains the sum of its row and column headers. This gives the completed table shown in the short answer, with $36$ equally likely ordered outcomes."
