      {
        "id": "p13-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Highlight the reduced sample space if the sum of the two dice is 5.",
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "answer": {
          "short": "Highlight the four cells for $(1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1)$.",
          "worked": "The cells with sum $5$ are $1+4$, $2+3$, $3+2$ and $4+1$. Highlight these four cells in the table from part a. The reduced sample space is $\\{(1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1)\\}$."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Given that the sum of the two dice is 5, what is the probability that:",
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p13-q14-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the first die shows a 1,",
            "answerSpaceMm": 18,
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac14$",
              "worked": "Of the four equally likely outcomes $(1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1)$, only $(1,4)$ has a first die of $1$.\n$$P(\\text{first die is }1\\mid\\text{sum is }5)=\\frac14.$$"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q14-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "at least one die shows a 1,",
            "answerSpaceMm": 18,
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac12$",
              "worked": "The favourable outcomes are $(1,4)$ and $(4,1)$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{at least one }1\\mid\\text{sum is }5)&=\\frac24\\\\&=\\frac12.\\end{aligned}$$"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "p13-q14-c-iii",
